      "new_informal": [
        {
          "id": "main",
          "text": "For real parameters $A,B,C,x_0$, the Vinogradov bound for $E_\\pi$ means that $E_\\pi(x)\\leq A(\\log x)^B\\exp\\!\\left(-C\\frac{(\\log x)^{3/5}}{(\\log\\log x)^{1/5}}\\right)$ for every real $x\\geq x_0$.",
          "origin": "later_upstream_natural_language_definition_instantiation",
          "role": "main_statement",
          "source": {
            "repository": "https://github.com/teorth/IEANTN",
            "commit": "0885c4e7bf9308ea11b40f2d79eda72ae00cb408",
            "path": "IEANTN/Vocabulary/ErrorTerms.lean",
            "url": "https://github.com/teorth/IEANTN/blob/0885c4e7bf9308ea11b40f2d79eda72ae00cb408/IEANTN/Vocabulary/ErrorTerms.lean#L76-L81",
            "retained_path": "reports/vinogradov-target-search-2026-11-09/sources/IEANTN/0885c4e7bf9308ea11b40f2d79eda72ae00cb408/IEANTN/Vocabulary/ErrorTerms.lean",
            "sha256": "f8f5be9702892e5b861e9b273946f02a13aa692eec11a4369b6db0db4f62bf34"
          },
          "scope": "This is a definition of a bound predicate, not an assertion that suitable constants exist. The parameters A, B, C and x₀ and the variable x are real. The quantified range is exactly every x ≥ x₀; there are no additional positivity hypotheses on A, B, C or x₀. The real functions and operations have the total conventions of the cited vocabulary, including exceptional inputs; no implicit restriction x₀ > 1 or x₀ ≥ 2 is imposed.",
          "targets": [
            {
              "file": "formal/Main.lean",
              "declaration": "Eπ.vinogradovBound",
              "relation": "describes"
            }
          ],
          "review_status": "model_reviewed_later_upstream_target"
        },
        {
          "id": "counting-and-integral-context",
          "text": "For a real variable $x$, $\\pi(x)$ is the number of primes at most $x$ (and is zero for $x<0$). The Riemann prime-counting function is $\\pi^*(x)=\\sum_{k\\geq 1}\\pi(x^{1/k})/k$. The offset logarithmic integral is $\\mathrm{Li}(x)=\\int_2^x dt/\\log t$.",
          "origin": "later_upstream_natural_language_definition_context",
          "role": "context",
          "source": {
            "repository": "https://github.com/teorth/IEANTN",
